 status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>DENSO CORPORATION</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>HANAKI, KENICHI</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NIPPON SOKEN, INC.</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NUNOGAKI, NAOCHIKA</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>YASUDA, ETURO</last-name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>HANAKI KENICHI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>NUNOGAKI NAOCHIKA</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>YASUDA ETURO</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>HANAKI, KENICHI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NUNOGAKI, NAOCHIKA</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>YASUDA, ETURO</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A piezoelectric multilayer body in which the displacement difference caused by application of electric field to the boundary between alternate electrode sections of an electrode central part of a unit multilayer body is decreased to a minimum by contriving the multilayer structure of an alternate electrode structure unit multilayer body.  Each of the piezoelectric element sheets (11a) of a unit multilayer body (10a) constituting the piezoelectric multilayer body integrally comprises an element sheet portion (11c) and ear portions (11d, 11e) and is made of a piezoelectric ceramic material.  An electrode layer (11b) is formed over the surface of the element sheet portion (11c) and the surface of the ear portion (11e).  The back of the upper multilayer sheet (11) out of the multilayer sheets (11) opposed to the electrode layer (11b) of the lower multilayer sheet (11).  The unit multilayer bodies (10a) are so stacked that the direction of each multilayer body is rotated by 90 degrees perpendicularly to the stack direction from the bottom to the top.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un corps multicouche piézoélectrique dans lequel la différence de déplacement induite par l'application d'un champ électrique sur la frontière entre deux sections d'électrode alternées d'une partie centrale électrode d'un corps multicouche est réduite au minimum au moyen de la structure multicouche de l'invention d'un corps multicouche unitaire de structure d'électrode alternée. Chaque feuille d'élément piézoélectrique (11a) d'un corps multicouche unitaire (10a) formant le corps multicouche piézoélectrique, est constituée d'une partie feuille (11c) d'élément et de parties oreilles (11d, 11e) et est fabriquée dans un matériau céramique piézoélectrique. Une couche électrode (11b) est formée sur la surface de la partie de feuille (11c) et la surface de la partie oreille (11e). Le dos de la feuille multicouche supérieur (11) est opposé à la couche électrode (11b) de la feuille inférieure (11). Les corps multicouches unitaires (10a) sont empilés de sorte que chaque corps multicouche soitourné de 90 DEG perpendiculairement à la direction de la pile, de bas en haut.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>